## API reference

### RevenueSummary

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `value:` | `Numeric` | - | Required. The period's total. |
| `title:` | `String` | `"Revenue"` | Label above the total. |
| `previous:` | `Numeric` | - | The previous period's total; adds the comparison and the trend badge. |
| `comparison:` | `String` | `"last period"` | Words after "vs $42,900". |
| `currency:` | `String` | `"USD"` | Currency for every amount in the card. |

Other attributes go to the card; `class:` is merged (set the width here). The badge carries `data-trend="up|down"`.

### Parts

| Part | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `RevenueMarkets(title: "Top markets")` | The market list. |
| `RevenueMarket(name:, value:, share:, country:)` | A row: flag (ISO code, e.g. `:us`), name, amount, share %. |
| `RevenueChart(data:, labels:, height: 76, aria_label:)` | A `Sparkline` line with gradient fill and hover tooltips. |
| `RevenueStats` / `RevenueStat(label:) { value }` | Key figures under a divider. |
| `CountryFlag(code, class:)` | Rounded flag; `us`, `de` and `jp` ship with the block, other codes show their letters. |

## Accessibility

- The chart is a labelled image (`aria_label:`), and its hover values are also readable as text in the tooltip.
- The trend is conveyed by the sign and the number, not only by the badge color.
- Flags are decorative (`aria-hidden`); the country name is always shown next to them.
